From 11f1dd36cd10a37aed5b0142afe42ef530a9a916 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: c4pp4
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 22:56:36 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/1] Keep the corner radius of menu windows

GTK publishes the corner radius of a menu window to Unity in the
_UNITY_GTK_BORDER_RADIUS property, and Unity draws the shadow of the
menu with these corners. The CSS that removes the rounding of windows
also applied to menu windows, so GTK published no radius and Unity drew
a square shadow around the rounded menus.

Leave out popup windows, they have no client-side decorations to remove.

Signed-off-by: c4pp4
---
 Source/GTK-NoCSD.c | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/Source/GTK-NoCSD.c b/Source/GTK-NoCSD.c
index d1679e9..4cf7ba0 100644
--- a/Source/GTK-NoCSD.c
+++ b/Source/GTK-NoCSD.c
@@ -2373,7 +2373,9 @@ int GTKNoCSDMagic(GtkWindow *Window, size_t Options) {
 
 			if (!GTKNoCSDNoCSS) {
 				// Remove rounding, padding, shadow, hide title
-				GTKNoCSDLoadCSS("window { border-radius: 0; box-shadow: none; }"
+				// Keep the corner radius of menu windows, GTK publishes it
+				// to Unity, which draws the shadow of the menu with it
+				GTKNoCSDLoadCSS("window:not(.popup) { border-radius: 0; box-shadow: none; }"
 					"headerbar { border-radius: 0; min-height: 0pt; padding: 0pt; }"
 					"headerbar * { margin: 0pt; }"
 					"decoration { margin: 0px; }"
